# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Pages serves HTML with max-age=0 but static assets with max-age=14400 (4 hours).
# That combination means that for four hours after a deploy, a returning visitor
# gets the NEW html paired with the OLD stylesheet and script from their browser
# cache. The page then renders wrong in ways that look like real bugs: the spam
# honeypot becomes a visible input, the privacy page loses its layout, and the
# contact form stops submitting in the background and dead-ends on Formspree.
#
# styles.css and script.js therefore revalidate on every request. That costs one
# conditional request each, which returns a ~200 byte 304 when nothing changed,
# and it makes every deploy correct immediately for everyone.
#
# Images keep a real cache. A stale image is cosmetic, never broken layout.

/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/script.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Security headers. Deliberately NO Content-Security-Policy here yet: this site
# loads fonts from Fontshare, posts the contact form to Formspree via fetch(),
# and has an edge-injected Cloudflare analytics beacon. A CSP has to allow all
# three, and getting connect-src wrong silently blocks form submissions. Worth
# adding, but only as its own change with the form tested against it.
#
# HSTS is set without includeSubDomains on purpose. The apex and www are the
# only hostnames this project controls; the other records point at Microsoft.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
